 Every night, observatories and space missions record far more than anyone has time to study. Open-Space downloads those public measurements, searches them with open code, and checks every lead against controls designed to catch false alarms. Each result comes with its data receipts, the scripts to replay it, and a plain statement of what it does *not* prove, so anyone can check our work.
 
-Between 13 and 15 November 2026 the project merged 95 contributions. The catalog below has 238 entries: 106 new measurements, 45 candidate discoveries, 20 forecasts of specific events, 24 corrections to published catalogs and papers, and 43 carefully recorded null or inconclusive checks. Entries below that carry none of these five labels (feasibility pilots, and analyses blocked because their data could not be retrieved) are listed for the record and are not counted.
